    dct:description "106 specimens x ~13 stages with per-specimen r / relative RMSE / ratio CV / BIC, genus means with bootstrap 95 % CIs, early/mid/late-third drift with Kruskal-Wallis p, KS of pooled residuals, Monte-Carlo gap test, two independent CV whorl ratios, Thompson's printed series refitted, and four controls through the identical rules — the pre-registered T1-T4 now discriminate (real data 3/4 vs shuffled 1/4 vs exact-geometric 4/4). Docked because the i.i.d. control is a boundary case rather than a true negative, KS rejects normality (honestly reported), and the T2 10 % drift limit is a pre-registered convention rather than a value Thompson stated." ;
